# armour/man/padded: the padded gambeson on the man (LADDER-ARMOUR, STYLE_P2 25.2 / 25.3 / 27.1-27.2): the hero's T1 coat,
# the herald's and the poor soldier's. The maker's cloth (cloth1) quilted: the STUFFED rows bulge a pixel past the seams and
# the step-1 quilt seams pinch in, every two rows, all straight; lit plane at the top-left (step 3, one step-4 shine on the
# lit shoulder), the turn step 2, the shadow side step 1; a high quilted collar with a clasp; a plain leather belt. Light
# weight: the civilian silhouette within a pixel. Plain, whole and honest: wear is the W region (a patch on the shadow
# shoulder, a stitched 2x2 at T1 by the finish tiles), never a hole.
# Finish regions: R the collar's rim and the hem, P the lit chest, G the collar clasp, N the quilt seams, W the patch.
# Keys: rest idle run runl drawn swing lie in D U R L. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. Source: LADDER-ARMOUR's expand.py.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR i3) the quilt softened: the lit side's seam rows a step up (8/7, not 8/6), so the T1 coat reads as stuffed
# cloth and not as bandage stripes; the shadow side keeps its flat step 1.
# (FORGE-TORSO round 2 i2) the quilt channels' N marks dropped (no finish rides them; the T1 coat stays plain at 1x).
use person
body man
role armour padded
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2
# (ladder i2, integration) the quilt in undyed buff (cloth3), not the tunic's cloth1: a gambeson over a same-colour
# tunic read as the bare tunic at 1x (C4 12 %); the T1 coat now reads as a coat
# (LADDER-ARMOUR polish i1, P3) the quilting runs DOWN the body in 3 px channels (a seam one step under its channel),
# the outline straight: the blind panel read the old horizontal bands as bandages / ribs.
legend 5 cloth3 0
legend 6 cloth3 1
legend 7 cloth3 2
legend 8 cloth3 3
legend 9 cloth3 4

